// L34 (REFERENCE.md): a `<~` slot writes its change back into the caller's
// variable. An expression gives it nowhere to write, and the write was silently
// lost — every engine accepted `bump(2 + 3)` and did nothing with the result.
//
// Since L36 the mark is required at the call site, so the mistake now has to be
// written `(2 + 3)<~`: the caller says the value comes back changed, and there
// is no variable for it to come back to.

bump(b<~) {
    b = b + 100
}

bump((2 + 3)<~)
